n we have that  connection and they know that i've been  there and they have been there and  together we can get them the help they  need  i've worked under  we've go under bridges in the desert  and that was the second year where i was  just starting to get back to where i was  supposed to be and where i went away  from  but all along knowing that  my job does not define who i am and what  i do doesn't define who i am i'm a  father  i'm a parent i'm a little league coach  i'm a friend i'm a sponsor  and i do a lot of things outside of my  work to protect my own sobriety and to  protect myself and what i'm doing so i  make sure that i never ever return  up until this point in the first to  second year i'm still living at a sober  living house because i felt like it  wasn't enough time  i needed to be sure that i was solid  so my wife and my kids she was living in  an apartment i was living in a sober  living house because i was just like i  don't know if we want to bring it back  together plus i'm still fighting and  working to get through this court battle  and the whole time trying to find a way  to talk to our children about it because  we just don't know what could happen  but i just wanted to just keep having  faith in knowing you know what i'm going  to stay clean and sober i'm going to  keep working with others i'm going to  keep making a difference in my community  i'm going to go out there and share my  story with as many people that can hear  what i'm saying to try and get them in  to change their lives  and the day was coming close  and we kept fighting my case and  fighting my case and i went to court  something like 20 25 times and this is  all in my cup recovery still to staying  clean and sober and still working with  others and hope that the judge would  have mercy on me  and i remember going back and forth to  court and it was just weighing on my  wife and weighing on my children and  my life coach troy was like mark just  hang in there and keep goi